// Title: DPAPI Backup Keys And Certificate Export Activity IOC
// Sigma ID: 7892ec59-c5bb-496d-8968-e5d210ca3ac4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nounou Mbeiri, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-06-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555, T1552.004
// Description: Detects file names with specific patterns seen generated and used by tools such as Mimikatz and
//   DSInternals related to exported or stolen DPAPI backup keys and certificates.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.dsinternals.com/en/dpapi-backup-key-theft-auditing/
//   - https://github.com/MichaelGrafnetter/DSInternals/blob/39ee8a69bbdc1cfd12c9afdd7513b4788c4895d4/Src/DSInternals.Common/Data/DPAPI/DPAPIBackupKey.cs#L28-L32
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_dpapi_backup_and_cert_export_ioc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "ntds_capi_" or FolderPath contains "ntds_legacy_" or FolderPath contains "ntds_unknown_") and (FolderPath endswith ".cer" or FolderPath endswith ".key" or FolderPath endswith ".pfx" or FolderPath endswith ".pvk")
